{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Then they shall give every man a ransom for his soul.</b> For the necessity of counting human persons arises from the change that occurs among them through coming-to-be and perishing, and this is caused by their sin, as they said: אֵין מִיתָה בְּלֹא חֵטְא (Shabbat 55a) — there is no death without sin. Therefore every counting recalls transgression; thus it is fitting that each one give a ransom for his soul to the honor of the blessed El, Who is merciful and will atone for transgression, as He says: לְכַפֵּר עַל נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶם. And for this reason He said [the following]." "<b>The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less.</b> For in this way a wealthy person is not distinguished before a poor one."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:35.907917942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}